# TypeScript

Follow skills **typescript** and **poteto-typescript** when applicable. Prefer pstack **typescript-best-practices** for modeling detail.

- `strict` + `noImplicitAny` on (including via `extends`); type-check in CI (`tsc -b` or equivalent)
- No unexplained `any` / `as any` / `as unknown as` / bare `@ts-ignore` / bare `@ts-expect-error`
- No postfix `!` on DOM queries or other external lookups; check at the boundary then use the narrowed value
- Parse external data (JSON, global fetch, URL, env, DOM) into a named domain type before trusting it; bare calls need `ts-rg-allow` on the named parser line. Method `.fetch` is allowed. Prefer `templates/env-schema.ts` / `templates/typed-parse.ts` starters.
- Prefer `unknown` at the parse site; `satisfies` over widening `as`
- Exhaustive `switch` with `never` default on discriminated unions (oxlint `switch-exhaustiveness-check`)
- Product public `.d.ts` must not expose `: any`; library host research may use `TS_RG_SKIP_DTS=1`
- Required product gates: `ts-rg-gate` + `ts-strict-gate` + `ts-runtime-gate` + `ts-oxlint-gate` + product lint/typecheck. Do not disable checks to force green.
- Prove emitted/runtime behaviour (drive smoke, unit, or playwright), not "types pass" alone

Repeated review smell twice on Control-Glass or other TS products: encode into lint/CI/skill, not more prose.
